    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2NbtoxptncnUmZRtU5iK66L)_\n\n## Merge order\n\n- Based on `main` after #498; touches only `sp-batch-report-view` (doc, tangled `.el`, tests).\n- No conflict expected with the open PRs. The next conversions of the other reports build on this, so merge this first.\n- Branch is `claude/project-thread-4a39fy`: the cloud proxy cannot rename a branch, so it needs the number prefix from Sia.\n\n## What changed\n\n- Table columns have a fixed width: as wide as the widest cell, at most `sp-batch-report-column-max-width` (40).\n  - The rest of a cell wraps inside its column, on the lines under it: at spaces, a long word is cut; links and faces stay.\n- When the columns do not fit the window, the widest are narrowed first, down to `sp-batch-report-column-min-width` (8), so no row runs off the window.\n- The width is counted in characters of the buffer's own text size, so zooming the text counts too.\n- The tables are laid out again by themselves, with nothing to press:\n  - triggers: `window-size-change-functions` (frame resize, split), `window-configuration-change-hook`, `text-scale-mode-hook`;\n  - it waits for 0.2 s idle, so dragging a frame edge draws once; nothing happens when the width is unchanged or the report has no table.\n- Drawing again keeps the folded sections, the dropped entries, the point (same row, same offset) and the top line of each window.\n- A row is still one entry for `n`/`p`, `d` and `u`.\n\n## Measured (batch Emacs 29.3, container)\n\n- 3000 table rows in 300 sections: first draw 0.50 s; draw again for a new width 0.58 s (once, after the resize stops).\n- Not measured: the GUI (frame drag, `text-scale-adjust`).\n\n## Tests\n\n- 6 new tests in `tests/sp-batch-report-view-test.el` (wrapping, widths, wrapped table, layout again keeps state, scheduling, lists need no layout); 17 pass, 1 skipped without Org.\n- Other test files: the only differences from before are Org-path tests that fail in the container because `goggles` (loaded from `org-mode-hook`) is missing; they need a run on the Mac.\n\n## Manual testing\n\n- [ ] Open `M-x sp-author-notes-bibtex` (tables): long titles wrap inside the Title column\n- [ ] Drag the frame narrower and wider: tables re-wrap on their own, after a short pause, with no key pressed\n- [ ] `C-x C-+` / `C-x C--` (text scale): the tables re-wrap for the new size\n- [ ] Fold a section, drop a few rows, then resize: folds and drops are kept and the point stays on its row\n- [ ] Split the window: the report in the narrower window re-wraps\n- [ ] A long list report (no table) does not flicker or re-draw on resize\n- [ ] Try `(setq sp-batch-report-column-max-width 25)` and re-open: columns are narrower\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9bi8g2P4sdH8GttsS)_",
